[[File:Aberrant spectre icon.png|left]]
'''Aberrant spectres''' are [[Slayer monsters]] that require level 60 [[Slayer]] to kill, and completion of [[Priest in Peril]] to receive as a [[Slayer task]]. They frequently drop large numbers of [[Herbs|grimy herbs]] and [[herb seed]]s. Because of this, bringing a [[herb sack]] and [[seed box]] when killing them is recommended.

[[Deviant spectre]]s, found in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], can be killed in their place if you are assigned aberrant spectres.

Wearing a [[nose peg]] or [[Slayer helmet]] is required when fighting aberrant spectres; otherwise they will use a special attack which will always hit, even through [[Protection Prayers]], and [[Temporary skill drain|drain your combat stats]] extremely quickly, in addition to other stats. Boosts cannot be used to equip a nose peg, so either level 60 Slayer or a Slayer helmet is required.

Aberrant spectres attack using [[Magic]], so using the [[Protect from Magic]] prayer or wearing magic resistant armour such as [[dragonhide armour|dragonhide]] is helpful. As they are [[undead]], the [[salve amulet]] can be worn for a damage and accuracy bonus when fighting them. The salve amulet's effects do not stack with those of a Slayer helmet when both are worn, in which case only the salve amulet effect will apply.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1242015573325877248|date=23 March 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/97403|archivedate=23 March 2020|quote=Salve effects override the Slayer helm / black mask effects (because they're either identical or bigger). So you'll get bonuses for Void, then multiplied up by the Salve effect, then multiplied up again for the dragonbane bonus.}} Regardless, players should still wear their Slayer helmet or nose peg to protect from the Spectres' unforgiving damage and stat drains.

